36. PUBLIC HEARING regarding a board approval and site plan for the
Leachman Feedyard and Sale Facility located in a portion of Sects 3,
4, 5, 6, 7, 9, 10, T18N, R61W and a portion of Sects 1, 2, 3, 10, 11,
12, T18N, R62W of the 6th PM, Laramie County, WY.
24 - 223
Leachman Feedyard and Sale Facility Board Approval
and Site Plan
Leachman Feedyard and Sale Facility PowerPoint
Attachments:
Cate Cundall, Planning, said Settje Agri-Services & Engineering, Inc, on behalf of
Leland Leachman, submitted applications for board approval and a site plan for the
Leachman Feedyard and Sale Facility. She said the property lies approximately half
mile southeast of Hwy 85 and Rd 152.  Cundall said the applications were submitted
to expand and operate a livestock feeding operation adjacent to their current facility at
5380 Rd 238. She said both applications were combined into one staff report for
ease of presentation and discussion, with separate motions required for the two
actions.
Leland Leachman and Travis Caspersen, applicant and agent, presented a
PowerPoint presentation of the operation. They said the purpose is to centralize
operations and provide a better regulatory environment in Wyoming.
Commissioner Thompson questioned Leachman and Caspersen about the process
for the odor footprint tool. Caspersen said he liked it and felt it was fair and not overly
burdensome, but it took a little time to figure it out because his company was the first
to use the tool since its adoption in 2020.
Cundall said based on evidence provided, staff recommends approval of the
